<section id="imagery">
    <h2>Imagery</h2>
    

    <h3>Multimedia Policies</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Text in Images:</strong> Splitli does not place text directly within images. Text that communicates key information is rendered in code rather than displayed in graphics so it remains readable by screen readers and can scale for users who enlarge text. Splitli’s guidelines for text in images include not placing essential instructions or navigation inside images, avoiding decorative typography, and having sufficient color contrast for any visible text inside images.</li>
        <li><strong>Video & Audio:</strong> Splitli does not use video or audio on its application. However, if it were to be implemented, all multimedia content must include accessible alternatives so users with hearing or visual impairments can fully understand the content. The video and audio guidelines include videos having synchronized closed captions, and audio-only content having a complete text transcript.</li>
        <li><strong>Motion Control:</strong> Motion and animations should support the user experience without causing accessibility barriers. Splitli limits the use of motion to subtle transitions and functional feedback. Our motion control guidelines include avoiding flashing content, not including animations that flash or blink more than three times per second, avoiding automatically playing videos or animations with sound, providing controls to pause, stop, and allowing user to disable motion when animations last longer than five seconds.</li>
    </ul>

